@startuml
title Gold Miner Fault Test Sequence Diagram

actor "Player" as P
participant "Client\nclient.py" as C
participant "Server\nserver.py" as S
participant "GameState\ngame.py" as G
participant "All Clients" as AC

P -> C : Press movement key
C -> S : PUSH move request\n(player_id, direction, seq)

note over C,S
Simulated fault:
network lag / delayed message
end note

... delay ...

S -> S : process delayed move\nin arrival order
S -> G : apply_move(player_id, direction)
G --> S : return updated state
S -> S : update last_move_seq[player_id]
S -> AC : PUB updated game state\n+ last_move_seq

C -> C : wait_for_my_move(seq)
C -> AC : render confirmed game state

note right of C
Client uses ZMQ RCVTIMEO.
If no state is received within 3000ms,
client reports possible crash or lag.
end note

note right of S
If messages are lost, only delivered moves are applied.
If messages arrive out of order, server processes them in arrival order.
If server crashes, clients stop receiving updates.
end note

@enduml